 34SI c  2010Ze03: a 100-MeV/nucleon {+34}P secondary beam was produced via     
 34SI2c  fragmentation of a {+40}Ar primary beam from the NSCL CCF impinging on 
 34SI3c  a 611-mg/cm{+2} Be target, separated by the A1900 fragment separator,  
 34SI4c  and impinged on a 2.6 mg/cm{+2} {+nat}Li (92.4% {+7}Li) target. |g rays
 34SI5c  were detected by SeGA array of fifteen 32-fold segmented Ge detectors. 
 34SI6c  {+34}Si nuclei were identified and momentum analyzed by the S800       
 34SI7c  spectrograph. Measured E|g with Doppler correction, I|g,               
 34SI8c  ({+34}Si)|g-coin, and angular distributions of scattered {+34}Si.      
 34SI9c  Deduced Gamow-Teller strength distributions from {+34}P to {+34}Si.    
 34SIAc  Comparisons with shell-model calculations.                             
